@context id=ctx001 seq=1 label="Git refs — first-class production content"
caption=|
	Git refs become first-class Vyasa content: discoverable, browsable, refreshable, and explicit about every outcome.
	Stage 40c is silent because existing controls need state behavior, not new screens or prototypes.
	Stage 80 stays in git; stage 90 waits until implementation is accepted.
@slides
vision: Why Git refs exist
	nodes=ask-1,gap-1,br-1
	desc=Repository history should read like live documentation, without changing a working tree.
failure: What breaks trust today
	nodes=fact-1,fact-2,fact-3,fact-4,fact-5,fact-6
	desc=The scoped mirror path is inert, failures collapse into 204, browser chains trust every response, and tests lock wiring rather than behavior.
contract: One truthful action contract
	nodes=fr-2,fr-3,fr-4,nfr-1,if-1,state-1
	desc=Every action has one result shape and five visible states: loading, updated, unchanged, viewing, or failed.
architecture: Put behavior where it belongs
	nodes=el-1,el-2,el-3,el-4,ad-1
	desc=Fetcher reports facts, coordinator owns refresh, extension owns routes and assets, browser behavior leaves global scripts.
delivery: Build and proof order
	nodes=wi-1,wi-2,wi-3,wi-4,tc-1,tc-2,tc-3,tc-4,tc-5
	desc=Server truth first, browser truth second, contract tests throughout.
